+// The memory of the main CPU at an address, as the game reads it. A bank must be followed: Williams System 7 runs its first page
+// (0x0000 to 0x00FF) on a bank of its RAM at 0x1000, and memory_find_base gives the page under the bank, which nothing ever writes.
+// No pointer means a read handler (se.c routes all Whitestar/Sega main RAM through ram_r): the memory behind it is at the base.
+static const uint8_t* MemMapFindBase(const unsigned int offset)
+{
+   const void* const ptr = memory_get_read_ptr(0, offset);
+   return static_cast<const uint8_t*>(ptr != nullptr ? ptr : memory_find_base(0, offset));
+}
